    "summary": "Kente cloth, composed of 4 strips of rayon (or possibly silk), hand-woven and hand sewn together along the selvedges. The warp is of yellow, red, black, white and green threads arranged in stripes in the &#039;Oyoko&#039; clan pattern. A weft chequerboard pattern has been formed along the central area of the cloth of two blocks of colour that flank geometric patterns in discontinuous supplementary weft. At both ends of the cloth is a variant pattern with six narrower bands of design that run across all four strips. The warp ends have been left as a fringe.",
